{
  "arguments": [
    {
      "id": "G13",
      "name": "Cross-Resolution Method",
      "speaker": "Framework author",
      "conclusion": "Every major claim must be read in its proper register (theology, physics, mathematics, lived reality, bridge) with no hidden upgrades.",
      "premises": [
        "Physics may not smuggle in theology; theology may not rescue weak physics.",
        "Story may not pretend it is proof; formal proof may not pretend to capture lived experience.",
        "When the same structure appears across registers, we mark the bridge, name its strength, state its limits, and keep testing.",
        "No hidden upgrades."
      ],
      "strength": {
        "st1": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "The Cross-Resolution Method requires every major claim to be read in the register where it belongs"
        },
        "st2": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "Physics is not allowed to smuggle in theology. Theology is not allowed to rescue weak physics. Story is not allowed to pretend it is proof. Formal proof is not allowed to pretend it has captured the whole meaning of lived experience."
        },
        "st3": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st4": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "But when the same structure appears across registers, we do not dismiss it merely because it crosses a boundary. We mark the bridge, name its strength, state its limits, and keep testing."
        },
        "st5": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st6": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "We mark the bridge, name its strength, state its limits, and keep testing. No hidden upgrades."
        },
        "st7": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "The framework names its own kill conditions in advance"
        },
        "st8": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        }
      },
      "prior_art": "none known (methodological regress-guard proposals in analytic theology, e.g. Nancey Murphy, Theology in the Age of Scientific Reasoning, 1990)",
      "originality": {
        "or1": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "The Cross-Resolution Method requires every major claim to be read in the register where it belongs",
          "why": "A variant on non-overlapping-magisteria / integrated-register methodologies rather than a wholly new methodological argument."
        },
        "or2": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "or3": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "when the same structure appears across registers, we do not dismiss it merely because it crosses a boundary",
          "why": "Uses a bridge register across theology, physics, mathematics and lived reality, but the cross-domain move is left abstract with no worked instance."
        },
        "or4": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        }
      },
      "weakest_link": "The 'bridge' register is defined by assertion: no criterion is given for when a cross-register structural resemblance is a real bridge rather than an analogy.",
      "develop_next": "State a checkable criterion (and a worked example) for when a cross-register structure counts as a bridge rather than a coincidence.",
      "case_map": ["K06"],
      "domain": "philosophy"
    },
    {
      "id": "G14",
      "name": "Necessary ground argument",
      "speaker": "Framework author",
      "conclusion": "The source sustaining the universe must be necessary, self-grounding, origin of coherence, active, and personal, which matches classical divine attributes.",
      "premises": [
        "If closed systems collapse and the universe has not collapsed, something external sustains it.",
        "If coherence and decoherence are real, measurable, and universal, the source of coherence must be equally real and universal.",
        "The required properties are: necessary, self-grounding, origin of coherence, active (passive maintenance is thermodynamically impossible), and personal (only persons ground moral facts).",
        "These properties map to aseity, self-sufficiency, eternality, omnipresence, Logos, providence, and personhood."
      ],
      "strength": {
        "st1": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "Those properties have had a name for thousands of years"
        },
        "st2": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "1. **Necessary** -- it cannot not exist, or the system collapses. 2. **Self-grounding** -- it cannot depend on something else (infinite regress). 3. **Origin of coherence** -- it must be the source of truth, order, beauty, goodness, life. 4. **Active** -- passive maintenance is thermodynamically impossible (the Second Law). 5. **Personal** -- only persons can ground moral facts (moral realism)."
        },
        "st3": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "If closed systems collapse and the universe has not collapsed, then something external sustains it."
        },
        "st4": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": "If coherence and decoherence are real, measurable, and universal, then the source of coherence must be equally real and universal."
        },
        "st5": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st6": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": "We started from five mathematical proofs and arrived at the exact description theologians have been writing about since the beginning."
        },
        "st7": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st8": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "If closed systems collapse and the universe has not collapsed, then something external sustains it. If coherence and decoherence are real, measurable, and universal, then the source of coherence must be equally real and universal."
        }
      },
      "prior_art": "Thomas Aquinas, Five Ways (Summa Theologiae I, q.2), c. 1265-1274",
      "originality": {
        "or1": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "Those properties have had a name for thousands of years",
          "why": "A variant of the classical necessary-ground / cosmological argument re-expressed with five 'mathematical requirements'."
        },
        "or2": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "If coherence and decoherence are real, measurable, and universal, then the source of coherence must be equally real and universal.",
          "why": "Adds decoherence/coherence language as evidence, though it is asserted rather than documented."
        },
        "or3": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "passive maintenance is thermodynamically impossible (the Second Law)",
          "why": "Bridges thermodynamics into theology by making the Second Law the reason the ground must be actively sustaining."
        },
        "or4": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        }
      },
      "weakest_link": "The premise 'only persons can ground moral facts' -- it is asserted with a parenthetical label and carries the entire move from abstract ground to a personal God.",
      "develop_next": "Defend moral-realism-plus-personal-ground with an actual argument, and supply the promised five proofs rather than citing them.",
      "case_map": ["K02", "K13", "K05"],
      "domain": "philosophy"
    },
    {
      "id": "G15",
      "name": "The Descent: 24-step causal chain",
      "speaker": "Framework author",
      "conclusion": "Being, followed all the way down through 24 steps, arrives at the Cross.",
      "premises": [
        "God creates; creation stands; what stands is distinguishable; distinction makes being intelligible; intelligibility carries information; information can stand in relation.",
        "Relation can be kept or broken, revealing value; value opens moral valence; moral valence makes right and wrong meaningful; right and wrong require choosing agents.",
        "Choice requires a world of rules, limits, time, and consequences, permitting decay and adversarial refusal.",
        "Adversarial action creates debt; perfect Justice and Mercy together require a cost-bearing source beyond the damaged order; that source is Grace; Christ is the convergence point."
      ],
      "strength": {
        "st1": {
          "v": 2,
          "quote": "Being, followed all the way down, arrives at the Cross."
        },
        "st2": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "God creates. Creation stands. What stands is distinguishable. Distinction makes being intelligible."
        },
        "st3": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st4": {
          "v": 1,
          "quote": "Adversarial action creates real debt, damage, and disorder. Perfect Justice requires that this be truthfully answered and paid. Perfect Mercy wills restoration rather than abandonment. Justice and Mercy together require a cost-bearing source beyond the damaged order itself."
        },
        "st5": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": ""
        },
        "st6": {
          "v": 0,
          "quote": "No premise smuggled. No step skipped."
